Hi,

A while ago we agreed to create a openvpn-commits list for GitHub's
commit notifications. We actually had the list already, but it was a
private list used to notify buildbot of commits via SF.net Git
post-receive hooks. Now the  list is public and open for subscriptions:

<http://sourceforge.net/mail/?group_id=3D48978>

The address of this read-only list is
"openvpn-commits@lists.sourceforge.net". Old SF.net Git post-receive
hook is still active, but once GitHub starts sending mails to the list,
it should be deactivated to avoid double-posting.

Let me know what configuration the list needs and I'll take care of it.

